    "math_academy_id": "q-124259",
    "knowledge_point_id": "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51",
    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form",
    "problem": "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv+3,\\,y=-9u+cv+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ -9u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3 \\\\ -9u+4v+4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=1u+0v+3,\\,y=-9u+4v+4\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+0+4=5.\n$$",
